WEBVTT

01:18.578 --> 01:21.331
BASED ON THE TRUE STORY OF GO PLAYERS
CHO HOON-HYUN AND LEE CHANG-HO.

01:21.414 --> 01:24.000
ALL CHARACTERS AND EVENTS
MAY DIFFER FROM REAL-LIFE COUNTERPARTS.

01:25.502 --> 01:27.670
THE YING SHIBEI WORLD GO CHAMPIONSHIP
WAS HELD IN THE 1980S

01:27.754 --> 01:28.922
TO FIND THE WORLD CHAMPION.

01:29.005 --> 01:30.840
ONE SPOT WAS GIVEN TO KOREA,
AN UNDERDOG COUNTRY.

01:30.924 --> 01:33.093
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN ADVANCED
TO THE FINAL AGAINST EXPECTATIONS.

01:33.176 --> 01:35.678
HIS OPPONENT, NIE WEIPING 9-DAN OF CHINA,
KNOWN AS "THE BLACK BEAR OF THE CONTINENT"

01:35.762 --> 01:37.680
WON THE CHINA-JAPAN SUPER LEAGUE
11 CONSECUTIVE TIMES

01:37.764 --> 01:38.932
AND WAS THE WORLD'S BEST PLAYER.

01:40.475 --> 01:45.313
The last round of the first Ying Shibei
World Professional Go Championship Final

01:45.396 --> 01:47.732
will be held in Singapore today.

01:47.816 --> 01:50.985
Korea's Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan
and China's Nie Weiping 9-dan,

01:51.069 --> 01:52.821
tied at two wins and two losses each,

01:52.904 --> 01:56.783
will battle in the match of the century
to become the King of Go.

01:57.283 --> 02:00.245
White has won all the previous rounds,

02:00.328 --> 02:04.457
so there's great interest
in who'll be white in the final round.

02:04.541 --> 02:05.959
He's here.

02:06.042 --> 02:08.795
A word, please.

02:08.878 --> 02:11.131
Mr. Cho, how are you feeling?

02:11.214 --> 02:12.966
How did you prepare for today's match?

02:14.008 --> 02:15.426
What if you choose black?

02:15.510 --> 02:17.929
-Are you going to attack fiercely?
-Nie Weiping!

02:19.931 --> 02:20.849
Piss off to Korea!

02:20.932 --> 02:25.603
China will definitely win!

02:26.521 --> 02:29.941
MATCH VENUE
STAMFORD HOTEL, SINGAPORE

02:39.659 --> 02:41.494
Nie Weiping 9-dan, white.

02:42.453 --> 02:44.372
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan, black.

02:59.804 --> 03:01.306
Let the match begin.

03:02.932 --> 03:05.602
THE 1ST YING SHIBEI
WORLD GO CHAMPIONSHIP FINAL, LAST ROUND

03:05.685 --> 03:08.688
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS NIE WEIPING 9-DAN

03:36.507 --> 03:41.346
THE MATCH

03:41.429 --> 03:45.934
Korea's Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan has ascended
to the top of the international Go scene.

03:46.017 --> 03:49.437
Cho defeated not only Japan,
which boasts of being

03:49.520 --> 03:51.439
the center of the world Go scene,

03:51.522 --> 03:54.025
but China, where Go originated,

03:54.108 --> 03:58.238
and his victory proves that the quality
of Korean Go is top-class.

03:58.821 --> 03:59.864
Right now,

04:00.448 --> 04:03.952
I feel like I couldn't lose
to the God of Go himself.

04:04.035 --> 04:06.537
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan,
the Go world champion,

04:06.621 --> 04:07.747
returned to Korea today.

04:07.830 --> 04:10.583
Cho 9-dan took part in a unique parade
from Gimpo Airport

04:10.667 --> 04:13.544
to the Korea Baduk Association
located in Jongno 2-ga.

04:13.628 --> 04:15.713
The government has decided to award Cho

04:15.797 --> 04:18.299
with the Eungwan Order of Culture Merit

04:18.383 --> 04:21.386
for improving the prestige
of Korean Go throughout the world.

04:22.845 --> 04:26.766
5 MONTHS LATER

04:26.849 --> 04:30.853
ONE-ON-MANY TEACHING MATCH
WITH PROFESSIONAL GO PLAYERS

04:36.067 --> 04:37.402
This kid is something.

04:37.485 --> 04:40.071
Didn't he solve
the life-and-death problem earlier?

04:40.154 --> 04:41.739
-What?
-From earlier.

04:41.823 --> 04:43.741
Gramps, this way.

04:46.411 --> 04:47.412
-Let's go.
-Okay.

04:47.495 --> 04:50.581
Look at this!
You're in a tight spot, Mr. Cheon.

04:50.665 --> 04:52.083
Look at you sweating.

04:52.166 --> 04:55.503
He's a Go prodigy in Jeonju.

04:55.586 --> 04:58.131
-He started less than six months ago.
-Six months?

04:58.214 --> 05:02.302
I heard he's unmatched in Jeonju,
no, in the entire Jeolla Province.

05:02.385 --> 05:03.761
-That's right.
-Hey.

05:03.845 --> 05:06.014
I think it's over. Why don't we stop here?

05:07.432 --> 05:08.599
Hold on, darn it.

05:12.145 --> 05:14.147
-I don't think it's over yet.
-What?

05:15.648 --> 05:18.151
You're wrong. It's over.

05:18.234 --> 05:20.069
If you don't mind, can I step in?

05:21.070 --> 05:22.530
Yes!

05:39.422 --> 05:41.257
What? It's an atari.

05:41.341 --> 05:43.217
YOU MAY CAPTURE THE OPPONENT'S STONE
ON THE NEXT MOVE

05:43.301 --> 05:44.302
He's been hit hard.

05:44.385 --> 05:45.887
Call it a tie and stop here?

05:51.851 --> 05:53.728
Wow, that's amazing.

05:53.811 --> 05:56.230
He's as good as I expected!
He turned it around.

05:57.106 --> 05:59.567
He's a champion for a reason.

06:00.526 --> 06:03.529
It's harder to win
when you have an advantage.

06:06.908 --> 06:08.826
I went too easy on him.

06:09.369 --> 06:11.120
Play another round.

06:11.204 --> 06:12.622
What's with you?

06:12.705 --> 06:14.916
Don't be rude, little kid.

06:14.999 --> 06:16.542
Go play over there.

06:16.626 --> 06:18.252
Stay out of this, novice.

06:19.504 --> 06:21.172
Come on. I want one more round.

06:21.255 --> 06:23.466
I'll win if we play again.

06:24.801 --> 06:25.635
What's your name?

06:27.261 --> 06:28.262
It's Chang-ho.

06:28.763 --> 06:29.597
Lee Chang-ho.

06:32.225 --> 06:33.559
Come on, sit here.

06:35.478 --> 06:36.479
Chang-ho.

06:38.064 --> 06:39.982
I heard you're good with life-and-deaths.

06:40.066 --> 06:43.069
WHEN A PLAYER CAN SAVE THEIR STONES
OR KILL THE OPPONENT'S STONES.

06:46.072 --> 06:47.407
Find black's lifeline.

06:48.032 --> 06:51.160
If you solve this,
I'll play another match with you.

06:51.244 --> 06:52.745
Do you mean it?

06:53.329 --> 06:54.664
Keep your promise.

06:55.540 --> 06:57.291
You can't take it back.

06:58.751 --> 07:00.420
He's a Lee from Gyeongju, like me.

07:00.503 --> 07:03.005
A family elder kept talking about him,

07:03.089 --> 07:05.675
so I told him to bring the boy.

07:06.217 --> 07:08.219
Well, he's good for a kid.

07:10.638 --> 07:14.475
That little kid has quite a temper.
Is he your nephew?

07:14.559 --> 07:16.644
I just met him for the first time.

07:16.727 --> 07:20.815
The family tree is all messed up.
He's actually a generation above me.

07:20.898 --> 07:23.734
Looks like I have a young uncle now.

07:25.278 --> 07:26.529
How many handicap stones?

07:29.740 --> 07:31.826
Four stones against a pro in six months?

07:31.909 --> 07:34.203
Did you say "black's lifeline"? Not white?

07:34.287 --> 07:36.205
Did you make a mistake, Mr. Cho?

07:36.289 --> 07:37.999
A mistake? Me?

07:38.082 --> 07:41.836
Why confuse him with a problem
that has no answer?

07:41.919 --> 07:44.046
There are no definite answers in Go.

07:45.214 --> 07:46.883
I've never seen a play like this.

07:47.467 --> 07:50.636
His haengma and opening are all mixed up…

07:50.720 --> 07:51.888
HAENGMA: THE SHAPE OF STONES

07:51.971 --> 07:53.014
…but it's oddly powerful.

07:53.097 --> 07:55.183
OPENING: OPENING TACTIC TO GET ADVANTAGE.

08:06.986 --> 08:09.780
-Did you solve it this time?
-I think he can do it.

08:09.864 --> 08:11.616
Bend and push.

08:11.699 --> 08:13.784
No, here. There, I mean--

08:13.868 --> 08:14.952
Come on.

08:15.453 --> 08:17.038
Gosh. You're so distracting.

08:17.121 --> 08:20.416
I told you I had to concentrate today.

08:20.917 --> 08:23.252
If you stare at me,
I can't get anything done.

08:23.336 --> 08:24.921
You're right.

08:25.004 --> 08:27.340
He needs to focus on this important work,

08:27.423 --> 08:31.093
so let's step out and have a drink.

08:31.177 --> 08:33.513
-Drinks are on me.
-We got scolded by him.

08:33.596 --> 08:36.516
If I drink during the day,
I'm going to pass out again.

08:37.183 --> 08:38.392
That kid…

08:38.476 --> 08:39.727
Don't you have homework?

08:40.311 --> 08:42.063
Are you going to sit there all day?

08:49.862 --> 08:52.949
He's the only son in three generations,
and he adores him.

08:53.699 --> 08:57.203
Humor him and say the boy's good,
that he shows talent.

08:57.286 --> 08:59.288
I'll take care of the rest.

09:04.377 --> 09:06.546
Amazing, isn't it?

09:06.629 --> 09:09.215
What a vigorous style from a young man.

09:09.715 --> 09:11.634
I'm 1-kyu in Go,

09:12.301 --> 09:15.388
and I'm lucky to win
one out of ten matches with him.

09:15.471 --> 09:19.225
Everyone keeps saying he's a prodigy,
filling him up with hot air.

09:20.226 --> 09:23.813
He's so into this silly game of stones
that he's ignoring the family business.

09:25.731 --> 09:29.569
Go's stature has risen recently
thanks to Champion Cho here.

09:29.652 --> 09:31.988
There are more international competitions,

09:32.071 --> 09:35.241
and you can contribute to Korea's
global reputation through it too.

09:37.159 --> 09:38.828
-You think so?
-Sure.

09:41.038 --> 09:42.290
That being said,

09:42.373 --> 09:44.208
I was hoping

09:44.292 --> 09:48.379
you could take the boy on
for a few months, Mr. Cho.

09:48.462 --> 09:50.798
I would compensate you handsomely

09:50.881 --> 09:53.217
and sponsor you magnanimously too.

09:54.051 --> 09:57.346
Use that money for his studies
so he can run the family business.

09:57.430 --> 09:59.140
That would be better for him.

09:59.223 --> 10:01.726
You don't get better at Go
by working hard.

10:03.519 --> 10:05.771
No point in training him
unless he's a genius.

10:06.772 --> 10:07.607
Talent?

10:09.191 --> 10:10.192
He doesn't have it.

10:10.860 --> 10:12.194
Not a trace of it.

10:15.823 --> 10:16.824
Cho!

10:18.200 --> 10:19.035
Cho!

10:20.369 --> 10:21.704
Hey! Cho Hoon-hyun!

10:23.414 --> 10:26.000
I've worked for months
to get that meeting.

10:26.083 --> 10:29.045
Do you know how much money
he can give us as a sponsor?

10:29.128 --> 10:30.713
What are we, beggars?

10:31.213 --> 10:34.091
Business meetings, sponsorships,
they're all fine.

10:34.175 --> 10:36.093
But let's not put money before Go.

10:36.802 --> 10:38.638
He called it "silly game of stones"!

10:39.388 --> 10:40.556
Don't you have any pride?

10:41.223 --> 10:42.058
Pride?

11:00.159 --> 11:01.327
Min-je.

11:01.911 --> 11:03.663
Cho Min-je, what are you doing?

11:04.163 --> 11:05.665
-Cho Min-je!
-Daddy!

11:07.333 --> 11:08.417
You're home.

11:08.501 --> 11:10.252
-Yeah.
-I made this for you.

11:10.336 --> 11:14.090
-Hey! I told you not to touch the mail.
-Did you?

11:14.173 --> 11:15.925
No, leave it. I'll tidy it up.

11:16.008 --> 11:18.010
-Come here.
-Is the mail that interesting?

11:18.094 --> 11:21.931
Come on. Let's wash our hands and eat.

11:22.014 --> 11:24.350
Could you turn on the gas stove?

11:24.433 --> 11:25.351
Let's go up.

11:25.851 --> 11:27.269
I want sausages.

11:27.978 --> 11:29.980
You had some this morning.

11:33.943 --> 11:35.903
KEEP YOUR PROMISE
FROM LEE CHANG-HO

11:43.828 --> 11:44.662
Hello.

11:44.745 --> 11:46.872
Hey, Lee. Cho Hoon-hyun speaking.

11:46.956 --> 11:48.374
Oh, hey.

11:48.457 --> 11:49.875
That boy, Chang-ho?

11:50.543 --> 11:52.128
Could I meet him again?

11:53.212 --> 11:54.714
Come on, let's go.

11:54.797 --> 11:56.048
Hurry.

11:56.757 --> 11:59.593
SORRY, WE'RE CLOSED TODAY.

12:03.097 --> 12:05.182
I'll only use three handicap stones.

12:05.266 --> 12:07.727
But if I win, you have to teach me Go.

12:09.520 --> 12:10.855
Why me?

12:10.938 --> 12:13.023
I heard you're the strongest player,
mister.

12:13.566 --> 12:15.151
That you're the best in Korea.

12:15.234 --> 12:16.068
Hey!

12:16.777 --> 12:20.781
Best in Korea? Try the best in the world.
You have no clue about what's going on.

12:21.365 --> 12:23.284
Hey. The masters are talking.

12:23.367 --> 12:25.453
Why does a novice keep interrupting?

12:25.953 --> 12:28.622
Look just how rude this little brat is.

12:28.706 --> 12:31.876
Last time, I only lost
because I gave you four handicap stones.

12:31.959 --> 12:34.253
I'd knock you out in an even game.

12:35.045 --> 12:37.214
You want to win against a kid that badly?

12:41.051 --> 12:42.052
What if you lose?

12:43.387 --> 12:44.805
What will you do for me?

12:50.019 --> 12:50.936
BANANA MILK

12:54.440 --> 12:55.441
Fine.

12:57.276 --> 13:00.070
Cho Hoon-hyun came all the way down here.
It's a done deal.

13:00.154 --> 13:02.364
What a smart son you have.

13:02.448 --> 13:03.449
Hey.

13:03.532 --> 13:05.534
Don't stand there. Come here.

13:06.494 --> 13:08.454
Look at him on pins and needles.

13:29.517 --> 13:32.019
I can't seem to make
my way around the board here.

13:32.102 --> 13:34.230
It's over for real this time, right?

13:34.855 --> 13:38.025
Yes, I lost this match.
You've gotten much better.

13:42.446 --> 13:44.031
You must be hungry.

13:45.282 --> 13:47.451
But who won?

13:47.535 --> 13:49.036
Uncle Chang-ho just won.

13:49.119 --> 13:51.664
Goodness, he won!

13:54.834 --> 13:56.919
Uncle, are you going to play again?

13:57.002 --> 14:00.172
We each won a game.
I need to see this through.

14:00.881 --> 14:02.633
Chang-ho, do you find Go fun?

14:02.716 --> 14:04.176
It's horrible.

14:04.677 --> 14:06.512
When I lose, I can't sleep or eat.

14:06.595 --> 14:08.722
It's the most infuriating thing
in the world.

14:08.806 --> 14:11.976
But when I win,
there's nothing more fun in the world.

14:13.185 --> 14:14.895
That's why we keep playing Go, right?

14:16.063 --> 14:17.314
That kid's an old soul.

14:19.441 --> 14:20.526
We'll finish the match…

14:23.153 --> 14:24.321
when you come to Seoul.

14:27.533 --> 14:28.701
-Well.
-Goodness.

14:31.120 --> 14:33.539
And don't call me "mister" like a novice.

14:33.622 --> 14:35.374
I'm not talking about you.

14:38.127 --> 14:39.753
I'm your teacher, so call me "sir."

14:40.796 --> 14:43.090
-Teacher?
-Good heavens.

14:43.799 --> 14:45.217
He did it!

14:45.801 --> 14:47.761
Chang-ho, what are you doing?

14:47.845 --> 14:50.723
Bow to your teacher now.

14:50.806 --> 14:52.641
-You don't have to.
-What?

14:52.725 --> 14:53.809
Let's not keep him!

14:53.893 --> 14:56.270
-This deserves a cheer.
-Hurray!

14:56.353 --> 14:57.855
Hurray for Korea's independence!

15:00.232 --> 15:03.694
You play three-day matches.
How are you going to handle a student?

15:04.194 --> 15:06.196
Where can you find the time to teach him?

15:06.697 --> 15:08.866
This is just between us,

15:08.949 --> 15:12.494
but you don't have
the right personality to teach anyone.

15:20.586 --> 15:22.838
Don't make more work for yourself.

15:22.922 --> 15:24.340
Just focus on your matches.

15:24.924 --> 15:27.426
What if he fails to become a pro?

15:27.927 --> 15:30.220
Tons of people
are just waiting to come at you.

15:30.304 --> 15:32.431
They'll say all sorts of things!

15:32.514 --> 15:34.350
I don't care about him becoming a pro.

15:38.020 --> 15:41.607
I suddenly became curious
about how his Go will turn out.

15:43.150 --> 15:48.447
Think of this as your grandpa
and wear it all the time.

15:48.530 --> 15:50.532
Since you're going to do this,

15:51.158 --> 15:52.993
go all in and leave no regrets.

15:53.702 --> 15:56.664
Go and do your best, okay?

15:57.581 --> 15:59.500
And listen to Mr. Cho.

16:00.960 --> 16:02.044
Okay?

16:03.629 --> 16:04.546
Okay.

16:30.656 --> 16:32.074
Mr. Cho.

16:32.157 --> 16:34.660
Goodness, you'll break the door.

16:34.743 --> 16:36.495
Hurry!

16:36.578 --> 16:38.080
The bathroom…

16:39.540 --> 16:40.791
Goodness.

16:43.502 --> 16:44.670
Welcome.

16:45.170 --> 16:47.089
It must've been a long journey. Come in.

16:56.598 --> 16:58.434
Man, I almost didn't make it.

17:00.269 --> 17:04.023
Oh my, what a handsome kid you are.

17:04.106 --> 17:06.525
Look at his thick bones
and wide shoulders.

17:06.608 --> 17:08.777
Sir, your wish came true.

17:08.861 --> 17:11.363
He has the perfect build
for a ssireum wrestler!

17:12.865 --> 17:15.117
-She's a girl.
-"She's a girl."

17:15.701 --> 17:17.786
Mrs. Cho, anyway, congratulations.

17:17.870 --> 17:20.080
You've got two babies at the same time.

17:21.040 --> 17:22.207
I guess you're right.

17:23.042 --> 17:24.960
-You're Chang-ho, right?
-Yes.

17:25.544 --> 17:26.378
Nice to meet you.

17:31.341 --> 17:33.010
This is the study.

17:34.428 --> 17:36.680
If you want to read anything,
help yourself.

17:49.526 --> 17:51.028
I was just about your age.

17:51.904 --> 17:53.822
Who's this old man?

17:54.656 --> 17:55.741
He was my teacher.

17:57.242 --> 17:58.410
Yikes.

17:58.494 --> 18:00.454
He looks terrifying.

18:01.246 --> 18:02.831
How old is he?

18:02.915 --> 18:04.500
He passed away a long time ago.

18:06.460 --> 18:08.629
Consider yourself lucky.

18:08.712 --> 18:10.547
I'm still young and energetic.

18:12.174 --> 18:15.427
My grandpa said
death doesn't care about your age.

18:19.389 --> 18:20.474
Come on out now.

18:22.017 --> 18:22.935
Come on.

18:26.063 --> 18:29.108
Is it because this is Igangju?
I don't feel drunk.

18:29.650 --> 18:31.693
It sure is
one of Joseon's top three liquors.

18:31.777 --> 18:35.614
Make sure to tell your grandfather
that I am grateful.

18:35.697 --> 18:38.200
-Yes, sir.
-Do you like the food?

18:38.283 --> 18:40.160
Yes, it's good.

18:40.244 --> 18:41.620
You're a good cook, ma'am.

18:43.664 --> 18:47.000
"Ma'am" doesn't sound quite right.

18:47.084 --> 18:48.168
I agree.

18:48.252 --> 18:51.255
We're family now.
You shouldn't call her that.

18:51.880 --> 18:53.715
I have to call her something.

18:54.299 --> 18:57.052
-I'm not sure how to address her.
-He's right.

18:57.136 --> 18:59.471
Once titles get mixed up,
your life can get…

19:00.389 --> 19:01.473
quite tricky.

19:04.977 --> 19:06.228
How about "Auntie"?

19:06.895 --> 19:09.356
Just call me "Auntie." Is that okay?

19:11.900 --> 19:12.734
Yes.

19:14.319 --> 19:16.155
Chang-ho, would you like more rice?

19:16.822 --> 19:17.739
Yes.

19:17.823 --> 19:19.908
A little more, please. Auntie.

19:21.952 --> 19:23.120
FUMIGATION

19:38.385 --> 19:40.053
KOREA BADUK ASSOCIATION

19:40.137 --> 19:43.932
CONGRATULATIONS
CHO HOON-HYUN CONQUERS THE WORLD

19:50.856 --> 19:53.442
Who are you? Are you looking for your dad?

19:53.525 --> 19:55.194
I'm not looking for anyone.

19:55.736 --> 19:57.988
I'm here to play Go.

19:58.071 --> 19:59.239
Go?

20:07.456 --> 20:08.457
Who's that kid?

20:09.541 --> 20:11.084
He's Champion Cho's student.

20:14.171 --> 20:15.672
Who's next?

20:18.050 --> 20:19.301
Hong-sik lost too?

20:19.384 --> 20:20.886
Seriously, he's no joke.

20:21.386 --> 20:22.471
He could be a pro.

20:25.515 --> 20:27.017
I haven't seen that shape before.

20:27.100 --> 20:28.769
He chose to push ahead?

20:28.852 --> 20:30.145
It doesn't make sense.

20:33.398 --> 20:35.317
Jeez, this is silly.

20:36.360 --> 20:39.780
I don't have time,
so just come at me all at once.

20:39.863 --> 20:41.365
Is he serious?

20:54.419 --> 20:57.547
He sure is a prodigy.

20:57.631 --> 21:00.634
Otherwise, why would've
Champion Cho brought him from Jeonju?

21:02.344 --> 21:05.097
Champion Cho found a good talent.

21:05.806 --> 21:07.557
-He's really good.
-He's something.

21:23.240 --> 21:24.783
Two territories here,

21:24.866 --> 21:27.369
and if you add the komi, it's at least 20.

21:28.036 --> 21:28.870
Keep going?

21:29.371 --> 21:32.916
SEJONG

21:33.000 --> 21:34.918
HOSTED BY KOREA BADUK ASSOCIATION

21:35.002 --> 21:37.254
THE 9TH GUKGIJEON CHALLENGE MATCH
4TH ROUND

21:37.337 --> 21:39.589
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS NAM GI-CHEOL 8-DAN

21:42.092 --> 21:44.344
Mr. Cho, you have 30 minutes left.

21:44.428 --> 21:46.346
FINAL MATCH BETWEEN
DEFENDING CHAMPION AND CHALLENGER.

21:50.350 --> 21:53.353
Champion Cho is brutally tenacious.

21:53.437 --> 21:56.273
Poring over a match
he's already won for 30 minutes?

21:56.356 --> 21:59.526
My respect goes to Expert Nam
for not throwing stones.

21:59.609 --> 22:03.196
This isn't the first time, and he knows
he'll eventually embarrass himself.

22:03.280 --> 22:05.949
I'm sick of this era of Cho and Nam.

22:06.825 --> 22:09.494
Mr. Nam, this is your final countdown.

22:10.078 --> 22:10.996
One,

22:11.580 --> 22:12.414
two,

22:12.998 --> 22:13.832
three,

22:14.750 --> 22:16.835
four, five,

22:17.753 --> 22:18.754
six,

22:19.338 --> 22:21.340
seven, eight,

22:22.174 --> 22:23.008
nine…

22:29.890 --> 22:31.433
What a bummer.

22:32.976 --> 22:34.728
I should've blocked it there.

22:37.689 --> 22:38.774
How stupid.

22:55.999 --> 22:56.833
There it is.

22:56.917 --> 22:58.001
The Tremor Technique.

22:58.543 --> 23:01.380
-What's that?
-How do you not know about that?

23:02.381 --> 23:05.801
If Cho Hoon-hyun starts bouncing his leg,
it's in the bag.

23:05.884 --> 23:10.305
In baseball, it's like Sun Dong-yol
warming up in the bullpen.

23:10.806 --> 23:13.016
It kills the opponent's spirit to fight.

23:16.561 --> 23:17.396
One,

23:18.021 --> 23:18.855
two,

23:19.606 --> 23:20.440
three,

23:21.066 --> 23:21.900
four…

23:21.983 --> 23:25.654
When the drizzle makes no sound

23:26.279 --> 23:30.450
We part at Busan Station in sorrow

23:32.119 --> 23:37.332
Goodbye, farewell

23:37.416 --> 23:40.669
There goes the whistle of tears

23:45.006 --> 23:47.551
A no-count win by Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan.

23:47.634 --> 23:49.886
A WIN SO DECISIVE
IT IS UNNECESSARY TO COUNT TERRITORIES.

23:50.470 --> 23:53.140
Oh boy, Expert Nam
seemed really angry today.

23:53.223 --> 23:56.893
Still, he should've put the stones back.
Such bad manners.

23:56.977 --> 23:59.896
Please, you're giving a lecture
on manners? "The drizzle"?

24:00.772 --> 24:03.692
You need to crush them
to make it easier the next time.

24:04.192 --> 24:06.778
Don't worry.
He'll be back, thirsty for revenge.

24:07.612 --> 24:11.366
Congratulations!
I heard your song choice was superb today.

24:11.908 --> 24:14.411
You bet. I can already see
the headlines tomorrow.

24:15.203 --> 24:18.540
Uncle Chang-ho is currently
sweeping through Gwancheol-dong.

24:18.623 --> 24:22.043
He's mowing down apprentices
like they're grass.

24:22.627 --> 24:24.921
They're talking about
the tiger cub you brought,

24:25.005 --> 24:26.673
and how he's a genius, a prodigy.

24:26.756 --> 24:27.674
Lee.

24:28.175 --> 24:31.595
You shouldn't tell Chang-ho
that he's a genius and a prodigy.

24:32.387 --> 24:33.638
It won't help him.

24:36.892 --> 24:37.976
Wait for me.

24:39.144 --> 24:40.061
Hello, sir.

24:41.980 --> 24:42.814
What's this?

24:43.607 --> 24:44.441
Candy.

24:45.525 --> 24:46.610
I'm home.

24:46.693 --> 24:47.861
You two came together.

24:49.070 --> 24:50.322
Yes, we met on the way.

24:50.405 --> 24:52.908
-Chang-ho, how did it go?
-Good, Auntie.

24:52.991 --> 24:54.659
How was the match today?

24:55.494 --> 24:56.495
I lost.

24:57.496 --> 24:58.747
You always say that.

25:03.793 --> 25:07.797
Your opening, haengma, and reading,
they're all terrible.

25:07.881 --> 25:09.925
But do you know what's the worst?

25:10.884 --> 25:12.636
Your bad attitude.

25:12.719 --> 25:13.637
What?

25:14.679 --> 25:16.264
But I beat everyone.

25:16.348 --> 25:18.934
Those older apprentices weren't that good.

25:19.017 --> 25:20.519
Winning isn't everything.

25:21.353 --> 25:23.355
Despite just starting to learn Go,

25:23.939 --> 25:26.149
you belittle those
who have studied for years?

25:26.233 --> 25:29.152
Your moves became lazy
when you were at an advantage.

25:29.236 --> 25:31.488
Do your best until the end.

25:32.030 --> 25:33.782
Learn to respect your opponents.

25:33.865 --> 25:35.534
What about you, sir?

25:36.243 --> 25:38.328
You bounce your leg and hum.

25:38.411 --> 25:39.246
You…

25:40.455 --> 25:41.873
Hey, I…

25:42.624 --> 25:43.625
I can't even…

25:44.125 --> 25:45.126
Why, you little…

25:47.462 --> 25:49.631
You can do that when you become the best.

25:51.174 --> 25:52.425
Unbelievable.

25:56.263 --> 25:57.639
Learn the basics first.

25:58.640 --> 26:00.058
But I've already read them.

26:00.642 --> 26:03.228
The standard patterns are boring,
and they're too easy.

26:03.311 --> 26:04.354
"Too easy"?

26:07.065 --> 26:08.441
Which side seems better?

26:08.525 --> 26:10.819
It's obvious white has the advantage.

26:16.408 --> 26:17.284
Take white.

26:25.083 --> 26:27.794
You don't come up
with a good move by thinking long.

26:27.877 --> 26:29.462
Thinking is for bad players.

26:30.255 --> 26:32.173
Cultivate a sense of the game.

26:33.174 --> 26:34.843
But don't play impulsively.

26:37.137 --> 26:38.471
Don't back down.

26:39.055 --> 26:41.224
The essence of Go
is the battle, the attack.

26:44.519 --> 26:45.937
Is white still better?

26:48.064 --> 26:49.065
No.

26:50.025 --> 26:51.026
Take black.

27:05.582 --> 27:09.002
I've only used the basics you belittle,
so why are you losing?

27:13.506 --> 27:16.176
"Genius, prodigy,"
don't believe what people call you.

27:17.093 --> 27:19.179
You're only good
at calculating and memorizing.

27:19.679 --> 27:21.598
You're only imitating how to play Go.

27:23.558 --> 27:25.143
Don't be cocky. Learn the basics.

27:29.606 --> 27:32.359
And use your right hand, if nothing else.

27:32.442 --> 27:34.903
It's a basic courtesy
to show your opponent.

27:36.321 --> 27:37.155
Yes, sir.

27:39.574 --> 27:41.076
Stamina is everything.

27:41.826 --> 27:43.578
The rashness of an impulsive move.

27:44.829 --> 27:47.415
The complacency of wanting to compromise.

27:48.208 --> 27:50.210
The arrogance
of wanting to end matches fast.

27:50.710 --> 27:53.630
These are things that happen
when your stamina fails,

27:54.339 --> 27:55.757
and they'll lead you to defeat.

28:07.769 --> 28:10.021
No, I'm going to use this hand.

28:21.908 --> 28:24.119
DEAR GRANDPA,
I HOPE YOU'RE WELL.

29:16.045 --> 29:18.423
ONE STEP, ONE MOVE

29:21.968 --> 29:24.804
Who eats jjajangmyeon on the rooftop?
Gotta be kidding me.

30:04.469 --> 30:05.303
Hello, sir.

30:05.386 --> 30:06.846
Why are you eating here?

30:09.849 --> 30:11.976
You couldn't have ordered together?

30:12.894 --> 30:15.897
I had to walk up here twice.
God, just eat at the restaurant.

30:18.775 --> 30:21.861
Champion Cho must work hard to feed you.

30:24.239 --> 30:25.073
Hey.

30:26.825 --> 30:28.326
You know who I am, right?

30:28.409 --> 30:30.495
Yes, of course. I do.

30:31.746 --> 30:34.833
You're Mr. Nam Gi-cheol,
my teacher's rival.

30:35.959 --> 30:36.960
Rival? Please.

30:39.838 --> 30:42.340
Don't relax because you became a pro,
and keep studying.

30:42.423 --> 30:44.217
Your teacher is extremely good.

30:44.300 --> 30:45.260
But,

30:46.845 --> 30:47.679
the thing is…

30:49.848 --> 30:52.684
I'm not sure if it's something
I can learn by studying.

30:54.394 --> 30:57.230
I wish I could be half as good as him,

30:59.023 --> 31:01.109
but I just don't seem to have it.

31:04.404 --> 31:05.655
Don't try to learn.

31:06.239 --> 31:07.490
Try to win.

31:09.367 --> 31:11.119
Then you'll naturally learn.

31:12.036 --> 31:13.997
That's what I did
when I played against Cho.

31:19.502 --> 31:22.881
CHO HOON-HYUN'S LEGENDARY MATCHES

31:22.964 --> 31:24.716
WHITE CHO HOON-HYUN
BLACK KIM SEONG-JU

31:32.557 --> 31:34.142
Man, he's so fast.

31:35.143 --> 31:37.061
How can I capture this?

31:38.313 --> 31:40.481
Going head-on won't help at all.

31:41.900 --> 31:43.401
Should I just hold my ground?

32:02.086 --> 32:05.089
Chang-ho's working hard into the night.

32:05.173 --> 32:06.007
Yeah.

32:07.258 --> 32:08.843
So, how's it going?

32:10.011 --> 32:11.596
The prelims start soon, right?

32:12.430 --> 32:15.183
How he does right now
is not what's important.

32:16.100 --> 32:17.685
It's about finding his own Go.

32:19.020 --> 32:21.189
Rushing him won't help.

32:21.981 --> 32:24.901
Don't just push him.
Coax and soothe him instead.

32:24.984 --> 32:25.902
He's still a kid.

32:25.985 --> 32:29.322
He won't come to anything if I baby him.

32:30.406 --> 32:31.824
He's someone's precious kid.

32:32.700 --> 32:35.536
I can't slack off.
I need to make him the best.

32:36.913 --> 32:40.166
In the world of competition,
if you're not the top dog,

32:41.376 --> 32:42.794
your life is too sad.

32:44.045 --> 32:47.006
THE 7TH DAEWANGJEON
1ST PRELIMINARY ROUND

33:23.126 --> 33:27.296
I mean, staring at the board
won't solve anything.

33:27.380 --> 33:28.548
You know what?

33:28.631 --> 33:31.426
I thought he fell asleep during the match.

33:32.093 --> 33:35.346
The kid plays Go like he's 60 years old.

33:35.847 --> 33:37.932
He's lost two rounds in a row.

33:38.599 --> 33:41.686
-How much did you lose, No?
-Two hundred thousand won.

33:42.520 --> 33:44.897
I'll lose all my tournament earnings
from this month.

33:45.857 --> 33:48.693
He's Cho Hoon-hyun's kid,
so I thought he'd be good.

33:49.277 --> 33:52.530
He was a bright kid.
Why is he getting worse?

33:53.031 --> 33:55.033
He's become totally weird too.

33:55.116 --> 33:59.120
Champion Cho must hound him
day and night with that temper of his.

33:59.203 --> 34:02.290
He's living with him too,
so it's no wonder.

34:05.376 --> 34:06.294
Grandpa.

34:07.211 --> 34:09.797
Mr. Cho's Go is flashy and strong,

34:09.881 --> 34:11.466
but it doesn't suit me.

34:12.175 --> 34:14.093
I'm going to find my own Go,

34:14.719 --> 34:18.639
something no one else can replicate,
even if it takes time.

34:21.017 --> 34:23.603
That's not it!
Upper right corner, knight's jump,

34:23.686 --> 34:25.980
attach the one at the top,
push, and extend.

34:26.064 --> 34:27.523
What have you learned so far?

34:27.607 --> 34:28.441
Honey.

34:29.400 --> 34:31.069
-Talk again tomorrow.
-Leave.

34:31.152 --> 34:32.904
He can't win all the time.

34:32.987 --> 34:35.573
He's upset about the loss,
so stop pushing him so hard.

34:35.656 --> 34:36.657
Just leave.

34:42.288 --> 34:45.541
You hold back when you should attack
and vice versa.

34:46.250 --> 34:47.251
Why are you offbeat?

34:48.961 --> 34:52.131
If a fight breaks out,
there would be more variables,

34:52.215 --> 34:54.050
so it'd be better to wait until later--

34:54.133 --> 34:54.967
I told you.

34:55.968 --> 34:58.971
Go isn't about compromising
and building territories.

34:59.472 --> 35:01.474
Bite, scratch, claw, and fight!

35:03.392 --> 35:06.062
That's your style, sir.
It's not right for me.

35:06.145 --> 35:07.271
Stop being cheeky.

35:07.355 --> 35:08.356
Style?

35:09.357 --> 35:10.441
A style of play?

35:10.983 --> 35:12.652
None of those matter if you lose.

35:13.277 --> 35:15.446
Use the basics.
Standard patterns come first.

35:17.615 --> 35:19.617
Does everyone need to play Go
the same way?

35:19.700 --> 35:21.911
There is an order to things!

35:22.662 --> 35:27.500
You need to have a reason for every attack
and for every retreat.

35:28.751 --> 35:29.752
You need the basics

35:29.836 --> 35:32.672
before you can make changes,
interpretations, and styles.

35:39.428 --> 35:40.429
It's the same here.

35:41.472 --> 35:45.726
It's only natural to extend over here,
so why would you retreat? Why?

35:46.811 --> 35:48.146
Are you openly defying me?

35:51.232 --> 35:54.986
It's the right move, but there's a chance

35:56.320 --> 35:57.822
that the tables might turn.

35:58.656 --> 36:01.159
But if I make this move,

36:02.243 --> 36:03.494
I'm 100% sure

36:05.454 --> 36:07.290
that I'll win at least half a point.

36:08.207 --> 36:09.125
100%?

36:09.917 --> 36:12.420
How many times have I told you
that it's difficult

36:13.087 --> 36:16.340
to claim territory in the center,
that it's hard to make calculations?

36:16.424 --> 36:18.176
You're right.

36:21.012 --> 36:23.681
But I thought
I could do the calculations, so…

36:25.725 --> 36:27.226
I did an experiment.

36:29.312 --> 36:30.479
"An experiment"?

36:33.316 --> 36:35.067
You think Go is just a silly game.

36:36.444 --> 36:39.280
You ignore the basics,
rely on your petty skill,

36:39.822 --> 36:41.490
and obstinately cling to your ideas.

36:46.037 --> 36:46.871
Let's stop.

36:48.039 --> 36:51.042
No reason to get angry at someone
who doesn't want to learn.

37:04.805 --> 37:05.640
But

37:06.432 --> 37:07.934
if I make this move,

37:08.601 --> 37:09.769
I'm 100% sure

37:11.520 --> 37:13.773
that I'll win at least half a point.

37:16.776 --> 37:19.278
Those who play first
have the advantage in Go.

37:20.279 --> 37:22.198
So, when playing someone of the same rank,

37:22.740 --> 37:25.076
the first player starts
with 5.5 points in the hole.

37:26.827 --> 37:28.079
That's called komi.

37:31.082 --> 37:34.252
The half-point here is given
to prevent a tie,

37:35.127 --> 37:38.464
and such a thing
does not actually exist on the board.

37:40.675 --> 37:42.677
The smallest unit that decides a match.

37:43.761 --> 37:46.305
Half a point,
which does not exist on the board.

37:47.431 --> 37:48.266
Perhaps,

37:49.392 --> 37:51.644
this kid is seeing something else here.

38:05.616 --> 38:07.618
RESPECTFULLY YOURS, CHANG-HO.

38:12.665 --> 38:15.668
SIR, AUNTIE, THANK YOU FOR EVERYTHING.
SORRY TO DISAPPOINT YOU.

38:22.883 --> 38:23.718
Where to?

38:25.136 --> 38:27.054
Jeonju, 9:40 bus, please.

38:27.138 --> 38:30.057
All right, 9:40 bus to Jeonju!

38:30.141 --> 38:32.059
The 9:40 bus is now leaving!

38:33.561 --> 38:35.396
Okay, anyone else boarding?

38:36.480 --> 38:37.815
Is everyone on board?

38:49.076 --> 38:49.910
Jeez.

38:50.911 --> 38:51.746
Sir?

39:08.637 --> 39:09.638
Yesterday,

39:11.265 --> 39:14.602
you talked about "half a point."

39:15.770 --> 39:18.939
It turns out you weren't completely wrong.

39:19.482 --> 39:21.317
But it wasn't right either.

39:21.817 --> 39:22.735
I just

39:24.320 --> 39:25.905
haven't found the right move yet.

39:32.703 --> 39:34.622
Go doesn't have answers,

39:36.374 --> 39:38.292
but I forced you to give me one.

39:40.544 --> 39:41.545
I'm sorry.

39:42.797 --> 39:44.215
It's better to walk steadily

39:45.049 --> 39:46.801
than to run and wobble.

39:48.469 --> 39:50.554
You found your own Go. That's good enough.

39:54.141 --> 39:55.810
If that is your decision,

39:56.394 --> 39:57.645
you need to own it.

39:58.729 --> 39:59.563
In both Go

40:00.648 --> 40:01.482
and life.

40:05.194 --> 40:06.278
Got it?

40:15.538 --> 40:17.540
Your spirit takes up 80% of a match.

40:19.041 --> 40:21.460
Even if you lose,
don't let them crush your spirit.

40:22.420 --> 40:23.421
Try to hide it.

40:24.171 --> 40:28.175
Your thoughts, emotions,
and even your breathing.

40:28.968 --> 40:31.137
Don't show your opponent anything.

40:31.887 --> 40:35.307
I know, but it's easier said than done.

40:36.267 --> 40:38.519
Think about something
familiar and comfortable.

40:40.104 --> 40:43.274
Something that relaxes you
just by thinking about it.

40:44.817 --> 40:47.653
The match is over
the moment you lose your composure.

40:54.076 --> 40:56.245
You shouldn't differentiate
the stones by color.

40:57.538 --> 40:59.623
Every move has to have a reason behind it.

41:00.249 --> 41:01.333
Territory

41:02.626 --> 41:05.337
comes into being naturally
and cannot be built with force.

41:06.797 --> 41:08.799
Take care of each and every stone.

41:10.134 --> 41:11.135
Then you'll find

41:11.969 --> 41:14.889
the stones have come into harmony.

41:17.683 --> 41:22.438
THE 29TH CHOEGOWIJEON
FINAL PRELIMINARY

41:26.358 --> 41:27.860
Cho, don't you have to be there?

41:27.943 --> 41:29.028
I don't have to.

41:29.612 --> 41:31.780
Poor Uncle Chang-ho.
Out of all those players,

41:31.864 --> 41:34.366
he had to meet Ko again,
the seasoned veteran.

41:35.242 --> 41:37.328
Hey, don't worry about him.

41:37.828 --> 41:40.414
You should all be figuring out
how not to be eaten by him.

41:40.998 --> 41:42.208
He's an odd one.

41:42.708 --> 41:48.047
He can't even review his games properly,
but he somehow keeps getting better.

41:49.215 --> 41:52.718
His opening is sloppy,
and his haengma is slow,

41:53.636 --> 41:55.346
but he somehow builds up a formation.

41:55.971 --> 41:59.725
When it comes to calculations,
he might be better than me.

41:59.808 --> 42:02.811
Does he still play like a 60-year-old man?

42:02.895 --> 42:03.896
No.

42:04.897 --> 42:05.898
Like an 80-year-old.

42:15.032 --> 42:17.284
I'd rather protect
half a point for certain

42:17.785 --> 42:20.120
than make a whole point through a fight.

42:21.497 --> 42:24.667
In the end, Go is a fight for territory.

42:26.293 --> 42:27.378
Grandpa.

42:27.920 --> 42:30.339
I think I've finally found my own Go.

42:30.965 --> 42:32.633
It's a bit unpolished

42:33.133 --> 42:35.219
and not flashy like Mr. Cho's,

42:35.719 --> 42:39.890
but I'm not going to let
anyone beat me, ever.

42:46.105 --> 42:48.524
Yeah, that's a good cut.

42:52.236 --> 42:56.073
The feng shui must be great
here at Yeonhui-dong, huh?

42:56.156 --> 42:58.909
You have two great pro Go players
under the same roof.

43:00.661 --> 43:02.913
Uncle, congratulations.

43:02.997 --> 43:05.916
You've made it to the finals already.
You're in good shape.

43:06.000 --> 43:09.336
Why don't we take a picture
to remember this day?

43:10.379 --> 43:13.465
Mr. Cheon, please take
a family picture for us.

43:14.592 --> 43:15.426
Of course.

43:22.349 --> 43:23.350
Here we go.

43:23.434 --> 43:24.768
One, two!

43:26.312 --> 43:27.730
Chang-ho. Come on, smile.

43:27.813 --> 43:29.064
Why do you look so glum?

43:29.898 --> 43:31.734
What? He's got that big smile on him.

43:31.817 --> 43:33.402
Yeah, he's smiling.

43:34.194 --> 43:35.529
-That's his smile?
-Yes.

43:37.031 --> 43:38.866
Okay, then. Here we go.

43:39.491 --> 43:41.827
One, two, three!

43:46.874 --> 43:48.208
But I think

43:49.418 --> 43:52.087
it'd be better for white
to bend this way here.

43:52.671 --> 43:54.715
It could win a lot,

43:55.924 --> 43:57.968
but it might leave an opening.

43:58.052 --> 43:59.970
Still, isn't it simpler to cut here?

44:03.599 --> 44:04.933
You're being too cautious

44:05.017 --> 44:06.935
that you're taking a long way around.

44:08.437 --> 44:09.772
I don't love it,

44:11.148 --> 44:14.318
but it doesn't seem
like it's going to give me a bad name.

44:15.527 --> 44:16.612
Who's next?

44:18.030 --> 44:19.406
Mr. Nam Gi-cheol.

44:21.492 --> 44:24.286
I'm worried too.

44:24.370 --> 44:26.789
His Go is so fierce.

44:26.872 --> 44:28.707
He's tenacious.

44:30.167 --> 44:33.337
If you start to back down,
he'll think you're weak and hit hard.

44:34.088 --> 44:35.589
Go strong from the beginning.

44:36.465 --> 44:38.300
I'm going for a hard defense.

44:39.301 --> 44:40.386
You punk…

44:41.637 --> 44:43.806
You told me to find my own Go.

44:43.889 --> 44:45.140
So I should butt out?

44:47.017 --> 44:48.268
Have faith in me.

44:49.520 --> 44:50.437
Okay.

44:51.355 --> 44:53.440
Think of it as a lesson, and take it easy.

44:54.608 --> 44:55.442
No.

44:58.195 --> 44:59.113
I'm planning

45:00.197 --> 45:01.615
to win.

45:03.867 --> 45:09.373
THE 23RD WANGWIJEON FINALS
12TH ROUND

45:22.720 --> 45:24.138
Nam Gi-cheol 9-dan, black.

45:24.722 --> 45:26.140
Lee Chang-ho 3-dan, white.

45:28.100 --> 45:29.435
Let the match begin.

45:29.518 --> 45:31.770
THE 29TH CHOEGOWIJEON
CHALLENGER SELECTION

45:31.854 --> 45:34.189
NAM GI-CHEOL 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 3-DAN

45:47.453 --> 45:48.370
Mr. Lee.

45:48.454 --> 45:49.788
Oh! My goodness.

45:49.872 --> 45:52.166
Why don't I get you coffee
in the review room?

45:52.249 --> 45:55.753
I'm good. I won't understand anything
even if I see it.

46:38.545 --> 46:41.423
Mr. Cho, you have ten minutes.

46:42.466 --> 46:43.634
Oh my!

46:44.343 --> 46:45.469
Let's see.

46:53.894 --> 46:54.978
Oh dear.

46:55.479 --> 46:58.065
A no-count win for white,
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan.

47:01.568 --> 47:02.736
Hey, Mr. Baek.

47:03.487 --> 47:04.822
I learned a lot from you.

47:07.950 --> 47:08.951
Hey, Cho.

47:10.661 --> 47:12.496
Black seems to have an advantage.

47:12.579 --> 47:14.706
Like you know anything.

47:14.790 --> 47:16.124
You got crushed too.

47:16.208 --> 47:19.294
I didn't get crushed, man.
I was still drunk that day.

47:19.378 --> 47:21.505
This is the record up to the 115th move.

47:39.523 --> 47:41.608
Maybe I shouldn't have cut it here.

47:42.776 --> 47:43.944
If I'd just taken it…

47:49.199 --> 47:52.703
I could've pushed one
and expanded to the center.

48:02.045 --> 48:04.798
A game between you and Champion Cho
would be interesting.

48:08.802 --> 48:10.637
You're better in the closing stages.

48:12.139 --> 48:13.056
Congrats, Lee.

48:19.771 --> 48:21.440
Expert Nam collapsed at the end.

48:21.523 --> 48:24.109
See? I'm not weak. Chang-ho's too strong.

48:24.943 --> 48:27.112
It must be the feng shui of Yeonhui-dong.

48:30.365 --> 48:32.492
LEE CHANG-HO

48:32.576 --> 48:33.410
CHALLENGER

48:34.411 --> 48:35.245
My.

48:42.669 --> 48:43.587
My, my.

48:44.421 --> 48:45.923
A teacher-student match…

48:46.673 --> 48:48.675
It's happening too soon.

48:48.759 --> 48:50.677
He earned his way up. What can I do?

48:52.054 --> 48:53.972
What if Chang-ho actually eats you up?

48:54.556 --> 48:55.390
Please.

48:56.266 --> 48:57.935
That's still ten years away.

49:03.649 --> 49:04.650
CITY HALL

49:13.617 --> 49:16.119
WINS THE YING SHIBEI CUP!
UNIFIES THE WORLD!

49:50.153 --> 49:51.738
CHO HOON-HYUN VS SEO GEON-WOO

49:57.661 --> 49:59.496
Mr. Cho's haengma is weak

50:00.080 --> 50:01.957
when attacked in the middle of a game.

50:05.085 --> 50:09.256
His check is always weak
when the shape expands.

50:16.471 --> 50:18.223
Sir, dinner's ready.

50:18.306 --> 50:19.141
Okay.

50:22.602 --> 50:24.271
Oh, here's the book.

50:39.703 --> 50:42.289
Come on, give him a pep talk.

50:42.372 --> 50:44.124
You are his teacher after all.

50:44.833 --> 50:46.001
What do you mean?

50:47.002 --> 50:49.588
Did you get some sleep?
How are you feeling?

50:49.671 --> 50:51.173
I'm good, Auntie.

50:52.799 --> 50:54.718
Don't get too hung up on the outcome.

50:56.678 --> 50:58.430
Just play your own Go.

51:01.308 --> 51:02.142
Yes, sir.

51:03.226 --> 51:04.311
CHALLENGE MATCH
LAST ROUND

51:04.394 --> 51:05.812
-Isn't that the car?
-They're here.

51:05.896 --> 51:07.355
FEBRUARY 2ND, 1990
KOREA BADUK ASSOCIATION, GWANCHEOL-DONG

51:07.439 --> 51:09.524
-They came together?
-Get a picture!

51:10.108 --> 51:12.360
-Mr. Cho!
-It's an unprecedented match.

51:12.444 --> 51:14.863
-How do you feel?
-Are you scared of your student?

51:14.946 --> 51:17.282
Goodness. What's the rush?

51:21.953 --> 51:22.788
Good luck.

51:23.663 --> 51:24.498
Thank you.

52:07.666 --> 52:08.875
We'll now choose stones.

52:24.099 --> 52:27.185
Lee Chang-ho 4-dan, black.
Cho Hoon-hyun 9-dan, white.

52:30.564 --> 52:32.149
Let the match begin.

52:33.775 --> 52:37.529
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 4-DAN

52:39.114 --> 52:40.490
COUNTDOWN

53:27.078 --> 53:27.913
Let's see.

53:27.996 --> 53:29.539
How many moves have been made?

53:29.623 --> 53:30.957
-Wait a minute.
-How is it?

53:31.041 --> 53:32.292
I just got it!

53:32.959 --> 53:34.544
-I haven't looked yet.
-Tell me!

53:34.628 --> 53:35.629
A little later!

53:37.255 --> 53:39.758
I'll tell you later, okay?

53:39.841 --> 53:40.884
God!

53:40.967 --> 53:42.552
What a racket. Seriously.

53:44.471 --> 53:46.723
That's a fierce opening from Cho.

53:46.806 --> 53:49.809
See? It's an onslaught from the beginning.

53:49.893 --> 53:54.064
How ruthless of him
against his young student.

53:54.147 --> 53:56.816
That is brutal. It really is.

54:13.166 --> 54:14.668
TIME SPENT

54:14.751 --> 54:18.004
LEE CHANG-HO 2 HOURS 10 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 50 MINUTES

54:24.761 --> 54:27.180
The game will resume after lunch.

54:31.351 --> 54:33.103
Should I have just taken it?

54:34.271 --> 54:37.023
A knight's cap,
and then a two-space extension.

54:39.859 --> 54:41.861
Maybe I should have given up a point.

54:48.576 --> 54:50.704
Great-grandfather, when did you get here?

54:51.496 --> 54:52.998
I took the first bus.

54:53.081 --> 54:53.915
Right.

54:55.375 --> 54:59.296
Chang-ho, you seem to be
off your game today.

54:59.379 --> 55:02.132
You were quite ruthless against me.

55:02.215 --> 55:04.050
Maybe he favors his teacher?

55:05.218 --> 55:07.637
Ask Mr. Cho to go easy on Uncle Chang-ho

55:07.721 --> 55:08.972
and cut him some slack.

55:09.556 --> 55:11.975
That's nonsense. A match is a match.

55:17.647 --> 55:18.648
He's such a…

55:21.776 --> 55:22.944
Good. The food is here.

55:26.823 --> 55:29.326
Careful now. It's hot. It's really hot.

55:29.409 --> 55:30.327
Goodness.

56:47.654 --> 56:51.366
Uncle Chang-ho seems to be making
a lot of small mistakes today.

56:51.449 --> 56:54.953
We can't compete with him either,
so how could a kid?

56:56.621 --> 56:58.623
And it's his teacher, whom he looks up to.

57:19.853 --> 57:21.020
TIME SPENT

57:21.104 --> 57:24.774
LEE CHANG-HO 3 HOURS 51 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 1 HOUR 43 MINUTES

57:33.199 --> 57:36.786
The match is over
the moment you lose your composure.

57:37.620 --> 57:39.789
Think about something
familiar and comfortable.

57:42.208 --> 57:44.627
Something that relaxes you
just by thinking about it.

01:00:03.725 --> 01:00:05.059
TIME SPENT

01:00:05.143 --> 01:00:08.980
LEE CHANG-HO 3 HOURS 53 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 2 HOURS 58 MINUTES

01:00:39.594 --> 01:00:40.595
Mr. Cho.

01:00:41.346 --> 01:00:42.180
One,

01:00:42.847 --> 01:00:43.681
two,

01:00:44.182 --> 01:00:45.183
three,

01:00:45.975 --> 01:00:46.809
four,

01:00:47.727 --> 01:00:48.561
five,

01:00:49.228 --> 01:00:50.063
six,

01:00:51.105 --> 01:00:51.939
seven,

01:00:52.523 --> 01:00:53.441
eight,

01:00:54.150 --> 01:00:54.984
nine,

01:00:55.652 --> 01:00:56.527
ten.

01:00:56.611 --> 01:00:59.989
LEE CHANG-HO 4 HOURS 50 MINUTES
CHO HOON-HYUN 5 HOURS

01:01:00.073 --> 01:01:03.159
Mr. Cho, you have two countdowns left.

01:02:13.813 --> 01:02:16.065
I don't know. We'll know when it ends.

01:02:16.149 --> 01:02:17.859
I might be wrong,

01:02:19.068 --> 01:02:20.987
but we might see a real coup here.

01:02:21.070 --> 01:02:21.988
A coup?

01:02:22.739 --> 01:02:23.573
Really?

01:02:25.241 --> 01:02:27.744
Why don't we go over there
and see for ourselves?

01:02:27.827 --> 01:02:29.746
Hey. Come on, hurry up.

01:02:29.829 --> 01:02:30.747
Hurry, run.

01:02:51.601 --> 01:02:52.518
Maybe not?

01:03:15.708 --> 01:03:17.460
Black wins by half a point!

01:03:17.543 --> 01:03:19.378
At 271 moves!

01:03:19.462 --> 01:03:21.214
Hey, I said black!

01:03:21.297 --> 01:03:22.465
No.

01:03:22.548 --> 01:03:24.467
Lee Chang-ho won!

01:03:43.820 --> 01:03:47.073
It's so late.
There won't be any restaurants open.

01:03:49.951 --> 01:03:50.785
Cho.

01:04:00.670 --> 01:04:03.130
A word on your student and his victory?

01:04:03.214 --> 01:04:04.882
Mr. Cho, can I get a comment?

01:04:09.595 --> 01:04:12.348
There's nothing more for me to teach him.

01:04:12.431 --> 01:04:14.433
He can go his own way now.

01:04:15.017 --> 01:04:16.894
What do you think went wrong today?

01:04:16.978 --> 01:04:18.354
-Sorry.
-Mr. Cho.

01:04:18.437 --> 01:04:19.814
Where was the match decided?

01:04:19.897 --> 01:04:22.900
You might face Mr. Lee in the Giseongjeon.
What's your plan?

01:04:22.984 --> 01:04:23.901
Mr. Cho!

01:04:32.535 --> 01:04:35.037
First of all, congratulations.
How do you feel?

01:04:36.289 --> 01:04:38.124
I'm sorry to my teacher

01:04:39.417 --> 01:04:41.002
that I won with a bad game.

01:05:33.220 --> 01:05:34.221
You're late.

01:05:38.351 --> 01:05:39.602
How did it go?

01:05:51.948 --> 01:05:53.532
Chang-ho, great job.

01:05:54.116 --> 01:05:55.034
Congratulations.

01:05:56.118 --> 01:05:57.119
Thank you.

01:05:57.703 --> 01:06:01.290
Good work. You must be tired.
Go up and rest.

01:06:02.541 --> 01:06:03.459
Okay.

01:06:13.844 --> 01:06:15.096
Grandpa.

01:06:16.389 --> 01:06:17.974
Did you see me win today?

01:06:20.059 --> 01:06:20.977
You know,

01:06:22.561 --> 01:06:24.313
I really wanted to win.

01:06:26.899 --> 01:06:27.984
In my own way.

01:07:07.606 --> 01:07:09.400
A HALF-POINT WIN
SENSATION IN THE WORLD OF GO

01:07:09.483 --> 01:07:10.568
YOUNGEST CHAMP, LEE CHANG-HO

01:07:12.445 --> 01:07:13.863
That boy…

01:07:46.145 --> 01:07:47.563
Should I have wedged it here?

01:08:02.620 --> 01:08:03.454
Hey.

01:08:03.954 --> 01:08:05.039
Sir.

01:08:07.166 --> 01:08:09.335
The review…

01:08:10.086 --> 01:08:11.337
Yes, we should do it.

01:08:11.420 --> 01:08:12.755
TO GO OVER MOVES FROM PAST GAMES.

01:08:12.838 --> 01:08:14.090
The weather's good.

01:08:15.091 --> 01:08:16.258
To the living room?

01:08:20.137 --> 01:08:23.307
What if I defend here?

01:08:23.891 --> 01:08:25.309
That's not bad either.

01:08:28.270 --> 01:08:29.688
But it's better to look here…

01:08:33.943 --> 01:08:37.279
and expand the center
because black is heavy.

01:08:44.453 --> 01:08:45.371
Or…

01:08:49.458 --> 01:08:50.835
what if I wedge it here?

01:09:06.267 --> 01:09:08.435
No, the shape doesn't look good there.

01:09:08.519 --> 01:09:12.022
You could defend this side instead

01:09:12.106 --> 01:09:15.317
or attach it here first.

01:09:17.570 --> 01:09:21.157
No, I don't think this is bad.

01:09:21.240 --> 01:09:24.743
Make an atari here, push through…

01:09:26.954 --> 01:09:27.872
and attach.

01:09:27.955 --> 01:09:31.667
No, not there. It leaves a bad aftertaste.

01:09:32.168 --> 01:09:34.086
No need to look any further.

01:09:38.507 --> 01:09:39.341
Sir.

01:09:45.347 --> 01:09:46.515
I'm sorry.

01:09:47.349 --> 01:09:50.269
About yesterday's game.

01:09:52.104 --> 01:09:52.938
What?

01:09:57.109 --> 01:09:58.944
Am I your teacher when we play Go?

01:10:00.988 --> 01:10:02.740
Answer me! Am I?

01:10:04.867 --> 01:10:05.701
No.

01:10:07.411 --> 01:10:08.329
You're my enemy.

01:10:08.412 --> 01:10:10.497
Winning a game doesn't change anything.

01:10:12.208 --> 01:10:13.626
Don't flatter yourself.

01:10:14.126 --> 01:10:17.129
You win and lose every day.
That's the fate of a pro.

01:10:17.213 --> 01:10:18.297
You arrogant punk.

01:10:20.549 --> 01:10:23.427
From now on, we won't review our games.

01:11:10.266 --> 01:11:12.893
THE 4TH GISEONGJEON CHALLENGE MATCH
LAST ROUND

01:11:12.977 --> 01:11:14.979
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 6-DAN

01:11:15.062 --> 01:11:16.981
The 27th teacher-student game.

01:11:17.064 --> 01:11:20.234
It's an earth-shattering event
that'll go down in Korean Go history.

01:11:20.317 --> 01:11:22.569
It's unprecedented, anytime, anywhere.

01:11:23.320 --> 01:11:25.906
Yes. Daewangjeon, Giseongjeon,

01:11:25.990 --> 01:11:30.077
Paewangjeon, Choegowijeon,
and now, Giwangjeon.

01:11:30.160 --> 01:11:34.039
The student and the teacher have met
in five consecutive final matches.

01:11:34.123 --> 01:11:36.792
This is all because of Lee Chang-ho 6-dan.

01:11:36.875 --> 01:11:38.377
He's growing too quickly.

01:11:38.460 --> 01:11:41.547
Cho 9-dan wouldn't have expected
him to rise so quickly either.

01:11:41.630 --> 01:11:45.134
Recent games show
that Cho is backed into a corner.

01:11:45.217 --> 01:11:47.970
Cho's knife is famous for its sharpness.

01:11:48.637 --> 01:11:50.639
It pierces and twists in your weak spots.

01:11:50.723 --> 01:11:52.224
But it doesn't seem

01:11:52.933 --> 01:11:55.019
to be working on Lee Chang-ho 6-dan.

01:11:55.102 --> 01:11:58.939
Yes, Lee 6-dan lets his opponent
do as he likes.

01:11:59.023 --> 01:12:01.942
But when you're done,
you find that you've lost.

01:12:02.026 --> 01:12:03.777
It leaves you dumbstruck.

01:12:03.861 --> 01:12:06.030
One professional player told me

01:12:06.113 --> 01:12:09.533
that he's scared to face Cho,
but as for Lee Chang-ho,

01:12:10.326 --> 01:12:12.494
he doesn't even want to look at him.

01:12:12.578 --> 01:12:16.081
As everyone knows, the two have
completely different playing styles.

01:12:16.623 --> 01:12:18.542
Cho is fast. Lee is slow.

01:12:18.625 --> 01:12:21.045
Lee holds back while Cho attacks.

01:12:21.754 --> 01:12:23.422
But looking at the game records,

01:12:23.922 --> 01:12:26.342
they seem to have switched their styles.

01:12:26.925 --> 01:12:30.179
It's the teacher, Cho 9-dan,
who has got his back to the wall,

01:12:30.679 --> 01:12:32.598
while Lee 6-dan is on the offense.

01:12:32.681 --> 01:12:36.435
It must mean that Cho is struggling
to change the flow by any means.

01:12:36.518 --> 01:12:38.687
Yes, but the problem is,

01:12:39.188 --> 01:12:41.815
Lee Chang-ho isn't just good at defense.

01:12:41.899 --> 01:12:44.485
He thoroughly punished Cho yesterday.

01:12:45.110 --> 01:12:47.863
Cho Hoon-hyun, the best player,
had his hands tied.

01:12:48.489 --> 01:12:50.574
-A comment, please!
-Mr. Cho!

01:12:50.657 --> 01:12:51.575
Mr. Cho!

01:12:53.869 --> 01:12:55.621
Mr. Lee, congratulations.

01:12:56.288 --> 01:12:57.706
Could you tell us how you feel?

01:12:57.790 --> 01:12:59.958
Where do you think the game was won?

01:13:00.042 --> 01:13:02.211
Only the Paewangjeon remains.

01:13:02.294 --> 01:13:06.382
If Cho loses there,
he'll end up with no wins this year.

01:13:06.924 --> 01:13:11.345
How do you all think
the next game will go?

01:13:11.428 --> 01:13:13.514
Lee Chang-ho is indeed in great spirits,

01:13:13.597 --> 01:13:16.600
but this is Cho Hoon-hyun, the King of Go.

01:13:16.683 --> 01:13:18.352
Well, he won't back down easily.

01:13:18.435 --> 01:13:19.520
Yes, that's right.

01:13:19.603 --> 01:13:22.314
If you look at Fujisawa 9-dan of Japan,

01:13:22.398 --> 01:13:25.401
he won a championship in his 60s.

01:13:25.484 --> 01:13:27.486
Don't be daft, you guys.

01:13:28.612 --> 01:13:30.531
There was no Lee Chang-ho in Japan!

01:13:30.614 --> 01:13:32.699
WINNER OF THE YING SHIBEI CUP!
UNIFIES THE WORLD!

01:13:36.745 --> 01:13:39.081
Lee Chang-ho is changing
the paradigm of Go.

01:13:39.665 --> 01:13:42.042
Go fans are even saying,

01:13:42.626 --> 01:13:44.878
"Go is a sport where you fight all day,

01:13:44.962 --> 01:13:47.381
only for Lee Chang-ho to win in the end."

01:13:49.967 --> 01:13:51.135
ETERNAL KINGDOM FALLEN BY HALF-POINT

01:13:51.218 --> 01:13:53.053
"SIR, IT'S PAEWANG THIS TIME"
CHO ON THE EDGE OF A CLIFF

01:13:53.137 --> 01:13:55.889
THE 29TH PAEWANGJEON CHALLENGE MATCH
4TH ROUND

01:13:55.973 --> 01:13:57.975
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 6-DAN

01:14:32.926 --> 01:14:33.927
Hey, Cho!

01:14:34.928 --> 01:14:36.263
Get the tissue.

01:14:50.777 --> 01:14:51.945
Mr. Cho?

01:14:52.905 --> 01:14:54.740
We'll get going now.

01:14:54.823 --> 01:14:57.159
All right. Have a safe trip home.

01:15:07.002 --> 01:15:08.921
This is terrible, really.

01:15:10.380 --> 01:15:11.882
For you and for Chang-ho.

01:15:33.862 --> 01:15:35.113
Is your stomach upset?

01:15:39.034 --> 01:15:40.202
I feel bad.

01:15:41.703 --> 01:15:43.455
For Mr. Cho…

01:15:45.958 --> 01:15:47.209
and Auntie.

01:15:50.462 --> 01:15:51.380
So,

01:15:52.881 --> 01:15:54.550
would you rather lose?

01:16:01.807 --> 01:16:03.475
Then give it your best and win.

01:16:04.810 --> 01:16:05.894
What else can you do?

01:16:41.179 --> 01:16:42.180
You're home.

01:16:53.567 --> 01:16:55.569
You couldn't even tie your shoes,

01:16:56.695 --> 01:16:59.031
and now, you look like a real pro.

01:17:06.371 --> 01:17:07.205
It's time…

01:17:09.708 --> 01:17:11.126
for you to stand alone.

01:17:13.211 --> 01:17:15.130
It makes no sense to keep you here

01:17:16.673 --> 01:17:19.343
as my student
when you've already surpassed me.

01:17:21.094 --> 01:17:25.349
No, I'm still not there yet.
I have so much left to learn.

01:17:26.642 --> 01:17:28.310
I have nothing to teach you.

01:17:31.480 --> 01:17:34.066
I should have sent you away sooner.

01:17:38.737 --> 01:17:41.406
Winning and losing
are part of our lives, yes…

01:17:43.992 --> 01:17:46.161
but to live in the same house like this,

01:17:47.829 --> 01:17:49.665
when we fight our guts out every day,

01:17:51.625 --> 01:17:53.043
is hard for both of us.

01:17:54.961 --> 01:17:56.963
I'm sorry, sir.

01:17:58.924 --> 01:18:00.008
Did I teach you that?

01:18:02.594 --> 01:18:06.098
A pro's job is to win,
no matter who the opponent is.

01:18:14.356 --> 01:18:16.692
I'm learning a lot lately, thanks to you.

01:18:18.443 --> 01:18:20.779
I've learned that I can lose at any time.

01:18:28.704 --> 01:18:30.038
I know you'll do well,

01:18:31.456 --> 01:18:33.291
but don't get lazy after leaving here.

01:18:48.390 --> 01:18:49.307
I realized…

01:18:51.560 --> 01:18:52.644
that I've never

01:18:53.603 --> 01:18:56.273
complimented you properly.

01:18:59.484 --> 01:19:00.485
As a teacher…

01:19:03.613 --> 01:19:05.449
I've always been proud of you.

01:19:08.577 --> 01:19:09.411
You were…

01:19:11.913 --> 01:19:13.081
always my pride.

01:19:32.851 --> 01:19:34.519
I packed some kimchi.

01:19:35.187 --> 01:19:36.354
Chang-ho likes it.

01:19:36.438 --> 01:19:37.939
Oh my, thank you.

01:19:38.857 --> 01:19:40.025
We're done.

01:19:42.068 --> 01:19:43.069
Chang-ho.

01:19:43.862 --> 01:19:44.780
Give me a hug.

01:19:46.615 --> 01:19:49.618
Come visit often. And don't skip meals.

01:19:52.037 --> 01:19:53.538
Yes, Auntie.

01:20:02.297 --> 01:20:05.634
Keep warm, and come by
for more side dishes when you run out.

01:20:05.717 --> 01:20:08.303
Sir, thank you so much for everything.

01:20:08.386 --> 01:20:09.554
It was nothing.

01:20:09.638 --> 01:20:10.639
Take care.

01:20:10.722 --> 01:20:13.058
Sure. Have a safe journey.

01:20:16.728 --> 01:20:17.646
Sir.

01:20:24.653 --> 01:20:25.570
Thank you

01:20:26.446 --> 01:20:27.697
for everything.

01:20:28.907 --> 01:20:29.741
Hey…

01:20:39.668 --> 01:20:41.920
Mr. Cho asked me to give you this.

01:20:59.271 --> 01:21:02.148
WHITE CHO HYEON-SIK VS BLACK LEE CHANG-HO
BLACK WINS BY 1.5 POINTS

01:21:42.147 --> 01:21:45.150
The Great Cho Hoon-hyun
without a single win, seriously?

01:21:45.233 --> 01:21:48.904
He was devoured by the tiger cub
he raised. Who can he blame?

01:21:49.404 --> 01:21:51.656
-Still, it does sting.
-It does.

01:21:51.740 --> 01:21:53.241
The truth is,

01:21:53.825 --> 01:21:56.661
we make more money when matches are tight.

01:21:56.745 --> 01:21:58.914
We won't make much commission like this.

01:21:59.748 --> 01:22:02.334
Lower the payout on Chang-ho.

01:22:03.752 --> 01:22:04.669
One,

01:22:04.753 --> 01:22:08.548
two, three, four, five,

01:22:09.257 --> 01:22:13.929
six, seven, eight, nine, ten.

01:22:16.097 --> 01:22:17.933
Cho of white runs out of time and loses.

01:22:18.683 --> 01:22:20.936
Nam of black wins by default.

01:22:49.297 --> 01:22:50.215
Where are the kids?

01:22:50.966 --> 01:22:52.717
-Aren't they home yet?
-No.

01:22:54.010 --> 01:22:55.261
How was the game?

01:22:56.596 --> 01:22:57.430
I lost.

01:22:58.932 --> 01:23:00.684
I can live with a loser,

01:23:02.060 --> 01:23:03.395
but not a pathetic man.

01:23:05.563 --> 01:23:06.982
Don't run like a coward.

01:23:09.985 --> 01:23:15.156
I've never resented you or Chang-ho once
while taking care of him,

01:23:16.700 --> 01:23:18.201
but seeing you like this

01:23:19.202 --> 01:23:20.787
makes me want to hate Chang-ho.

01:23:23.790 --> 01:23:25.375
Why are you so pathetic?

01:23:34.801 --> 01:23:37.053
Champion Lee, it's been a long time!

01:23:37.137 --> 01:23:38.304
Have you eaten?

01:23:38.388 --> 01:23:40.807
If not, why don't we have lunch together?

01:23:40.890 --> 01:23:43.143
No, I'm not hungry yet.

01:23:43.226 --> 01:23:44.561
I'm sure he's full.

01:23:45.061 --> 01:23:48.231
He gorged himself
on all those championship titles

01:23:48.314 --> 01:23:49.816
and gobbled up his teacher too.

01:23:50.316 --> 01:23:52.986
He didn't gobble up anything.
Watch your mouth, man!

01:23:53.069 --> 01:23:55.488
Why are you throwing a fit?

01:23:56.448 --> 01:23:58.033
It was a joke.

01:23:58.533 --> 01:23:59.451
Joke!

01:24:02.996 --> 01:24:05.165
It must be nice for you, Lee.

01:24:05.749 --> 01:24:07.500
Wow, you're photogenic too.

01:24:07.584 --> 01:24:09.753
ANOTHER FORFEIT
WILL CHO HOON-HYUN RETIRE?

01:24:11.129 --> 01:24:13.381
Wow, you could be a model.

01:24:16.801 --> 01:24:19.637
How about a bowl of naejangtang?
It's been a while.

01:24:19.721 --> 01:24:21.097
-Sure.
-Okay.

01:24:21.848 --> 01:24:24.184
-A drink too?
-What should I do, then?

01:24:29.105 --> 01:24:29.939
Me?

01:24:30.732 --> 01:24:33.318
What would you do, Mr. Baek,
if you were me?

01:24:34.903 --> 01:24:36.404
Should I lose?

01:24:36.988 --> 01:24:40.075
Well, why are you asking me that?

01:24:40.909 --> 01:24:43.995
That's what I was taught.

01:24:44.079 --> 01:24:46.247
That a pro's job is to win.

01:24:47.957 --> 01:24:51.294
You must not have met
a good teacher yet, Mr. Baek.

01:24:51.377 --> 01:24:52.712
You little…

01:24:53.755 --> 01:24:55.757
You think you're above everyone else now?

01:24:57.592 --> 01:24:58.510
It's a joke.

01:24:59.636 --> 01:25:01.221
I was joking too.

01:25:01.304 --> 01:25:02.514
What?

01:25:04.182 --> 01:25:05.183
He said it was a joke.

01:25:06.684 --> 01:25:08.186
Let's go now, Lee.

01:25:14.526 --> 01:25:16.778
A forfeit? The Great Cho Hoon-hyun?

01:25:17.403 --> 01:25:19.322
You should have at least played!

01:25:19.906 --> 01:25:22.242
Do you know
how much your wife worries about you?

01:25:23.618 --> 01:25:24.702
And Chang-ho?

01:25:25.286 --> 01:25:26.454
Poor kid.

01:25:27.497 --> 01:25:30.083
He might not talk about it,
but he must feel terrible.

01:25:37.549 --> 01:25:40.176
Hey, what are you doing?
You're a lightweight.

01:25:44.264 --> 01:25:45.265
Hey, Cho.

01:25:46.391 --> 01:25:47.225
What?

01:25:57.694 --> 01:25:59.362
My knife's gone rusty.

01:26:04.159 --> 01:26:05.410
You don't have an umbrella.

01:26:06.244 --> 01:26:07.495
Hey, Cho!

01:26:54.542 --> 01:26:56.878
CHO HOON-HYUN VS LEE CHANG-HO
NO-COUNT WIN BY LEE

01:27:12.810 --> 01:27:15.897
I'd be upset if you bowed down
to something as small as this.

01:27:18.816 --> 01:27:21.986
Because you've stabbed me in the back
at least a hundred times.

01:27:25.323 --> 01:27:27.408
Everyone hurts when they're punched.

01:27:29.410 --> 01:27:31.329
Chang-ho must be having a hard time too.

01:27:33.498 --> 01:27:34.999
The poor kid's suffering

01:27:36.334 --> 01:27:37.919
because he met a teacher like me.

01:27:39.587 --> 01:27:42.924
He's a champion, and he can't even smile
as much as he likes.

01:27:44.425 --> 01:27:46.344
You're still his teacher.

01:27:48.054 --> 01:27:51.057
You need to challenge him
so that he grows stronger.

01:27:53.851 --> 01:27:55.436
Go is so odd.

01:27:58.022 --> 01:27:59.524
Once you place a stone,

01:28:00.692 --> 01:28:02.694
you feel like you could do it…

01:28:04.862 --> 01:28:06.781
but it's hard to place it down.

01:28:11.369 --> 01:28:13.955
I thought I'd finally started
to understand the game.

01:28:16.374 --> 01:28:18.376
You win if you can overcome that.

01:28:20.086 --> 01:28:24.090
The aching wound oozes, scabs over,
and is covered with new flesh.

01:28:25.550 --> 01:28:26.884
You endure it…

01:28:29.637 --> 01:28:31.389
until an opportunity comes to you.

01:28:34.559 --> 01:28:35.476
Cho.

01:28:38.813 --> 01:28:41.399
I've found that once you start
running away on the board…

01:28:44.235 --> 01:28:45.903
there's nowhere else to go.

01:28:57.915 --> 01:28:59.167
Be yourself.

01:29:00.335 --> 01:29:02.253
Being quiet and hunched up like this

01:29:03.671 --> 01:29:05.089
doesn't suit you at all.

01:29:48.800 --> 01:29:51.636
GO IS ABOUT TRYING TO FIND AN ANSWER
WHEN THERE ARE NONE

01:29:51.719 --> 01:29:53.554
KENSAKU SEGOE (CHO HOON-HYUN'S MASTER)

01:30:15.451 --> 01:30:20.289
GO IS A FIGHT AGAINST YOURSELF
JULY 1964, CHO HOON-HYUN

01:30:24.001 --> 01:30:26.170
I'm stuffed. That was good.

01:30:26.671 --> 01:30:28.840
Mr. Baek, congrats on your easy win ahead.

01:30:28.923 --> 01:30:30.341
I didn't see Cho today.

01:30:30.425 --> 01:30:33.719
Don't congratulate me.
This is going to be an uncomfortable win.

01:30:33.803 --> 01:30:37.765
Now's the moment to face off
against Cho Hoon-hyun and crush him.

01:30:39.267 --> 01:30:41.352
He won't come. He's too scared.

01:30:45.523 --> 01:30:47.942
Mr. Baek, you're here.

01:30:48.693 --> 01:30:49.694
So,

01:30:50.278 --> 01:30:52.238
did you have a filling lunch?

01:30:55.867 --> 01:31:00.705
1 YEAR LATER

01:31:05.626 --> 01:31:07.712
THE 2ND WOMEN'S GUKSUJEON FINALS

01:31:07.795 --> 01:31:09.255
Sir?

01:31:09.839 --> 01:31:11.215
Look at you, kid.

01:31:11.299 --> 01:31:12.717
Here, let me.

01:31:13.301 --> 01:31:15.553
It's okay. I'll do it.

01:31:25.229 --> 01:31:26.147
Sir.

01:31:27.648 --> 01:31:28.816
Today's game…

01:31:29.567 --> 01:31:30.818
Of course I won!

01:31:32.653 --> 01:31:35.072
What are you asking me that for?
It's embarrassing.

01:31:36.908 --> 01:31:40.077
Look at me playing
in the preliminaries like some novice.

01:31:42.079 --> 01:31:43.581
I saw your game yesterday.

01:31:44.624 --> 01:31:47.376
So you're still not choosing to fight.

01:31:48.836 --> 01:31:51.005
Because I can win without fighting.

01:31:52.673 --> 01:31:56.010
Why risk it and fight?

01:31:56.511 --> 01:31:59.305
Or are you avoiding a fight
because you're scared?

01:31:59.805 --> 01:32:01.224
Of course not.

01:32:02.225 --> 01:32:03.976
Whose student do you think I am?

01:32:08.523 --> 01:32:11.776
Yeah. A master doesn't need
a lecture from a novice.

01:32:14.278 --> 01:32:16.280
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan wins a no-count win

01:32:16.364 --> 01:32:18.616
and succeeds in defending
his Daewangjeon title.

01:32:18.699 --> 01:32:22.036
He has 19 consecutive championship wins,
and if he wins…

01:32:22.119 --> 01:32:26.123
What matters is how many consecutive wins
Lee Chang-ho gets, right?

01:32:26.958 --> 01:32:28.376
Paewangjeon will be held…

01:32:28.459 --> 01:32:31.128
You don't have to watch it.
Lee will win three to zero.

01:32:31.212 --> 01:32:34.298
Cho Hoon-hyun is a has-been now.

01:32:34.382 --> 01:32:37.218
Cho 9-dan advanced
through a variety of preliminaries

01:32:37.301 --> 01:32:41.597
and finals and now will challenge
his old student, Lee Chang-ho 7-dan.

01:32:41.681 --> 01:32:42.765
Lee Chang-ho…

01:32:45.560 --> 01:32:46.727
-Hey, you're here.
-Hi.

01:32:47.228 --> 01:32:48.563
-Okay, all done.
-Okay.

01:32:49.647 --> 01:32:51.399
-Did you check the mic?
-Yes.

01:32:52.608 --> 01:32:53.526
Hey, Cho.

01:32:54.110 --> 01:32:55.695
Don't do it if you don't want to.

01:32:56.612 --> 01:32:57.446
Really?

01:33:00.199 --> 01:33:01.534
I'm joking.

01:33:01.617 --> 01:33:04.287
I'm not that shameless.
It's about time I did one.

01:33:04.954 --> 01:33:05.788
Go ahead.

01:33:08.749 --> 01:33:10.001
First, congratulations.

01:33:10.501 --> 01:33:15.798
You were voted the most popular Go player
by the fans last year.

01:33:15.881 --> 01:33:16.882
How do you feel?

01:33:16.966 --> 01:33:20.303
If I had known, I would have started
losing much sooner.

01:33:20.970 --> 01:33:24.056
When I was on a winning streak,
everyone hated me so much.

01:33:25.725 --> 01:33:26.559
Yes.

01:33:26.642 --> 01:33:28.227
Well, the records show

01:33:28.311 --> 01:33:31.480
you've played 110 matches
in the last year alone.

01:33:31.564 --> 01:33:34.567
You've been playing
practically once every three days,

01:33:34.650 --> 01:33:37.570
with all the preliminaries and the finals,

01:33:37.653 --> 01:33:41.240
when, in the past, you were used to
waiting as the defending champion.

01:33:41.824 --> 01:33:42.825
It's been rough.

01:33:45.036 --> 01:33:49.123
But it makes the match more exhilarating
when a single loss

01:33:50.082 --> 01:33:51.584
will send you down the cliff.

01:33:51.667 --> 01:33:53.336
It's been fun in a way.

01:33:53.419 --> 01:33:56.339
It was refreshing,
going against young rookies too.

01:33:58.633 --> 01:34:01.802
Well, Lee Chang-ho 7-dan is on a roll,
and everyone is saying

01:34:01.886 --> 01:34:03.971
that it's not news if he wins.

01:34:04.055 --> 01:34:05.890
Now, for your last question,

01:34:06.390 --> 01:34:10.895
could you send a message to Lee Chang-ho,
your student and opponent in the final?

01:34:16.734 --> 01:34:19.570
He might have been my student,
but a match is a match.

01:34:21.572 --> 01:34:23.991
If I have to fight Chang-ho,

01:34:25.242 --> 01:34:26.911
I plan on giving it my all.

01:34:28.245 --> 01:34:31.832
It's now my turn to challenge him
as he did me.

01:34:40.966 --> 01:34:42.301
CHO HOON-HYUN RETURNS!

01:35:07.118 --> 01:35:10.204
THE 31ST PAEWANGJEON CHALLENGE MATCH
LAST ROUND

01:35:10.287 --> 01:35:12.790
CHO HOON-HYUN 9-DAN VS LEE CHANG-HO 7-DAN

01:35:34.770 --> 01:35:37.940
It's the final game.
Both sides have two wins each.

01:35:38.023 --> 01:35:40.067
I thought it'd begin in a cautious manner,

01:35:40.151 --> 01:35:42.862
but it's going very quickly.

01:35:42.945 --> 01:35:46.866
The opening so far
is the same as the fourth match.

01:35:46.949 --> 01:35:48.451
It's as if it's choreographed.

01:35:48.534 --> 01:35:51.203
Yes, it's heated,
with neither side backing down.

01:35:51.287 --> 01:35:54.498
It's like they're both shouting
that their Go isn't wrong.

01:35:54.582 --> 01:35:58.878
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan
is known as the "God of Calculation."

01:35:58.961 --> 01:36:02.965
Cho 9-dan won the first two matches

01:36:03.048 --> 01:36:06.886
but lost the next two and is now perched
on the edge of a cliff.

01:36:06.969 --> 01:36:10.347
The teacher-student matches
have continued in this pattern,

01:36:10.431 --> 01:36:14.769
and comeback wins have become
Lee Chang-ho's signature.

01:36:14.852 --> 01:36:19.190
Cho's challenge is to keep
his composure until the end.

01:36:26.489 --> 01:36:27.740
Cho is playing elsewhere.

01:36:28.324 --> 01:36:31.035
It's customary to take
and strengthen here,

01:36:31.118 --> 01:36:33.329
but he just placed his stone here.

01:36:33.996 --> 01:36:36.665
Hasn't Cho's Go become
so much sharper and more acute

01:36:36.749 --> 01:36:39.418
since he's bounced back
after hitting rock bottom?

01:36:39.502 --> 01:36:42.838
Yes, it earned him a new moniker,
the "God of War."

01:36:42.922 --> 01:36:44.173
From that perspective,

01:36:44.256 --> 01:36:47.218
it seems Cho is planning
to incite a fight here and there.

01:36:47.301 --> 01:36:49.553
I'm curious how Lee 7-dan will respond.

01:36:51.639 --> 01:36:54.308
Wow, Lee Chang-ho 7-dan strikes back!

01:36:54.391 --> 01:36:55.810
He's out to capture his enemy.

01:36:55.893 --> 01:36:59.063
He has no intention of compromising today,
which is unusual.

01:36:59.814 --> 01:37:02.817
Cho sneers,
like he didn't expect this either.

01:37:21.001 --> 01:37:25.089
Lee Chang-ho strikes back
against Cho Hoon-hyun's wave of attacks!

01:37:27.925 --> 01:37:29.760
Cho shakes up the center.

01:37:30.636 --> 01:37:33.722
It doesn't seem like Lee Chang-ho
will have to rise to the attack.

01:37:37.643 --> 01:37:39.478
Wow, Lee Chang-ho!

01:37:39.979 --> 01:37:41.146
He jumped in!

01:37:41.856 --> 01:37:46.193
Neither gives their groups a glance.
All they care about is the battle!

01:37:47.361 --> 01:37:49.613
Neither the teacher nor the student

01:37:49.697 --> 01:37:52.950
will give an inch
when it comes to the match.

01:38:07.339 --> 01:38:09.592
The battle is truly chilling.

01:38:09.675 --> 01:38:12.011
They're fighting like sworn enemies.

01:38:16.557 --> 01:38:19.143
Lee is now taking a long pause.

01:38:20.060 --> 01:38:24.732
He's probably running tens of thousands
of possible sequences in his head.

01:38:46.962 --> 01:38:49.798
Lee Chang-ho makes a sharp thrust.

01:38:49.882 --> 01:38:52.051
Cho has to be aching.

01:38:53.594 --> 01:38:56.931
White seems to be
at an advantage in general.

01:38:57.014 --> 01:38:58.807
What do you think, Mr. Nam?

01:38:58.891 --> 01:39:01.977
Champion Cho has started fights
here and there,

01:39:03.145 --> 01:39:05.397
but Chang-ho's walls are just too thick.

01:39:05.481 --> 01:39:08.651
Yes, it seems like Lee is ahead
by three and a half

01:39:08.734 --> 01:39:11.070
or four and a half points so far.

01:39:11.862 --> 01:39:15.866
The game is entering its endgame.

01:39:16.367 --> 01:39:19.203
If Lee wins today,
he'll reenact his teacher's achievement,

01:39:19.286 --> 01:39:21.914
which is to win
all championships in a year.

01:39:22.414 --> 01:39:25.000
Lee Chang-ho 7-dan. You're almost there!

01:39:30.381 --> 01:39:34.051
He's making a counterattack
in an unlikely situation.

01:39:34.134 --> 01:39:36.887
Could it be that Cho
is planning to capture over here?

01:39:37.638 --> 01:39:39.056
It won't be easy.

01:39:39.556 --> 01:39:41.558
It's Lee Chang-ho he's facing.

01:39:43.143 --> 01:39:44.311
He's defended it well.

01:39:44.395 --> 01:39:46.605
It's Lee Chang-ho after all.
That's a good spot.

01:39:46.689 --> 01:39:50.526
Yes, he staged a defense
and went for his opponent's vital point.

01:39:51.360 --> 01:39:53.862
It's a classic Lee Chang-ho move.

01:39:55.823 --> 01:40:00.327
How will Cho, who's on the defensive,
get out of this difficult situation?

01:40:01.537 --> 01:40:05.457
He has never been
at an advantage during this game.

01:40:19.596 --> 01:40:22.933
What was that move by Cho?
Does that make any sense?

01:40:23.017 --> 01:40:25.269
What? He's going to jump in even more?

01:40:25.769 --> 01:40:28.188
Whoa, it's too reckless.

01:40:28.272 --> 01:40:30.107
I mean, there's nothing to back it.

01:40:40.868 --> 01:40:43.203
Did Lee just retreat?

01:40:44.288 --> 01:40:48.459
I think it'd be better
to bend here and capture one point.

01:40:49.251 --> 01:40:50.085
So what was that?

01:40:52.921 --> 01:40:56.550
Is there something more to Cho's move?

01:40:57.426 --> 01:40:59.011
I'm sorry. What did I miss?

01:40:59.094 --> 01:41:01.847
What could possibly be behind this move?

01:41:06.560 --> 01:41:09.396
Vital points are very tender.

01:41:11.565 --> 01:41:16.320
Once you get hit, you can't move.
You can only gasp.

01:41:19.656 --> 01:41:21.658
As more stones are placed and they mingle,

01:41:22.910 --> 01:41:24.578
it results in more vital points.

01:41:26.288 --> 01:41:28.749
My vital point is also

01:41:30.209 --> 01:41:31.710
that of my opponent.

01:41:35.172 --> 01:41:36.840
-Wait a second.
-Yes?

01:41:37.549 --> 01:41:39.301
I see. It's genius!

01:41:39.885 --> 01:41:42.471
Black retreats here,
and white makes an atari.

01:41:42.554 --> 01:41:44.973
Black connects,
then white needs to extend here.

01:41:45.474 --> 01:41:48.977
And in the end,
black will inevitably gain an advantage.

01:41:49.061 --> 01:41:51.605
It's an exquisite bid for victory by Cho!

01:41:51.688 --> 01:41:54.358
The teacher finally twists
the student's arm!

01:41:54.900 --> 01:41:58.403
If this works,
Cho might turn the game around.

01:41:59.613 --> 01:42:01.031
It takes two to play Go.

01:42:02.574 --> 01:42:06.662
A single genius cannot create
a good game of Go on his own.

01:42:08.539 --> 01:42:09.540
This match

01:42:10.040 --> 01:42:11.792
is one that will go down in history.

01:42:24.888 --> 01:42:26.974
Lee Chang-ho bends on the left side.

01:42:28.183 --> 01:42:29.768
Cho blocks decisively.

01:42:44.283 --> 01:42:46.785
The stone statue winces!

01:42:46.869 --> 01:42:48.704
So Lee Chang-ho is human too!

01:43:51.725 --> 01:43:53.227
Lee Chang-ho resigns!

01:43:53.310 --> 01:43:54.978
Cho Hoon-hyun has won!

01:43:55.062 --> 01:43:58.398
Lee Chang-ho is blocked
from a grand slam by his teacher!

01:43:59.566 --> 01:44:03.570
Cho Hoon-hyun got up again after 15 losses

01:44:04.071 --> 01:44:07.824
and has finally overcome the huge obstacle
that is Lee Chang-ho!

01:44:08.742 --> 01:44:13.080
Cho wins the Paewangjeon and escapes
his drought of no championship titles!

01:44:13.872 --> 01:44:14.957
Everyone!

01:44:15.040 --> 01:44:17.042
The King is back!

01:45:03.922 --> 01:45:04.756
WINNER

01:45:29.156 --> 01:45:30.407
Have a safe journey home.

01:45:32.159 --> 01:45:33.243
Here.

01:45:33.910 --> 01:45:34.745
This is…

01:45:34.828 --> 01:45:37.080
Well, it didn't feel right
to throw it out.

01:45:37.164 --> 01:45:39.249
It's still usable. Here.

01:45:46.006 --> 01:45:47.382
TAXI

01:45:47.966 --> 01:45:51.970
Cut, throw-in, bend,

01:45:52.846 --> 01:45:55.349
atari, cover…

01:46:19.831 --> 01:46:21.750
GO IS ABOUT TRYING TO FIND AN ANSWER
WHEN THERE ARE NONE

01:46:24.669 --> 01:46:29.174
GO IS A FIGHT AGAINST YOURSELF
JULY 1964, CHO HOON-HYUN

01:46:36.765 --> 01:46:41.603
NOVEMBER 16, 1998
THE 42ND GUKSUJEON EVE EVENT

01:46:42.020 --> 01:46:43.605
Now, let's wrap up the pictures

01:46:43.688 --> 01:46:45.357
and start the press conference.

01:46:45.440 --> 01:46:49.277
Reporters, could you please
move to your designated seats?

01:46:52.114 --> 01:46:57.035
First, the Guksu Champion title
has come to represent you in a way,

01:46:57.119 --> 01:46:59.287
so you must be very emotional right now.

01:46:59.830 --> 01:47:00.997
You take a title

01:47:02.124 --> 01:47:04.709
and have it taken away from you.
That's how it goes.

01:47:04.793 --> 01:47:06.962
Maybe it's my age, but these days,

01:47:07.671 --> 01:47:09.005
I'm more interested in…

01:47:12.342 --> 01:47:15.262
leaving behind a good game record
than winning a title.

01:47:15.345 --> 01:47:18.265
Mr. Cho, you've been on a roll recently.

01:47:18.849 --> 01:47:20.642
Is there a secret to it?

01:47:22.227 --> 01:47:23.228
Well…

01:47:26.022 --> 01:47:28.442
They say the sun shines

01:47:29.234 --> 01:47:31.820
the brightest before it sets.

01:47:34.364 --> 01:47:36.366
I expect it will subside soon.

01:47:37.742 --> 01:47:39.661
What's your take, Mr. Lee?

01:47:41.288 --> 01:47:43.039
Since he quit smoking,

01:47:43.123 --> 01:47:45.375
he stopped making mistakes
in the closing stages.

01:47:45.459 --> 01:47:47.169
It must've been the cigarettes.

01:47:49.004 --> 01:47:49.838
Thank you.

01:47:51.006 --> 01:47:55.927
Finally, could you both tell us
how you'll approach tomorrow's match?

01:47:58.889 --> 01:48:01.600
Chang-ho's gotten a taste
for comeback wins lately,

01:48:01.683 --> 01:48:03.977
which is probably
why he let me win the first game,

01:48:05.437 --> 01:48:09.107
but now that we're at it, I'll turn
tomorrow's match into another lesson.

01:48:11.651 --> 01:48:14.237
I think one loss was enough for a lesson.

01:48:16.156 --> 01:48:19.659
Many of you seem to be
rooting for Mr. Cho's victory,

01:48:20.243 --> 01:48:22.913
but I'm not willing to relinquish

01:48:23.705 --> 01:48:25.790
the hard-won champion title so easily.

01:48:50.440 --> 01:48:51.775
Chang-ho, it's you again?

01:48:55.111 --> 01:48:56.446
Yes, sir.

01:49:01.326 --> 01:49:02.410
It is what it is.

01:49:03.453 --> 01:49:04.704
This is what a match is.

01:49:11.753 --> 01:49:17.676
MUSHIM: TO EMPTY OUT ONE'S HEART

01:49:23.848 --> 01:49:29.771
SEONGEUI: TO GIVE ALL ONE'S HEART

01:50:23.617 --> 01:50:24.451
NOVEMBER 17, 1998

01:50:24.534 --> 01:50:26.703
CHO HOON-HYUN TOOK BACK
THE GUKSU CHAMPION TITLE, HIS SYMBOL

01:50:26.786 --> 01:50:29.039
FROM LEE CHANG-HO AFTER FIVE YEARS
ON THE DAY OF THE FIRST SNOW.

01:50:29.122 --> 01:50:30.206
THE FIRST SNOW FELL THAT DAY.

01:50:36.463 --> 01:50:39.299
LEE CHANG-HO RULED AT THE TOP
OF THE INTERNATIONAL GO SCENE FOR 15 YEARS

01:50:39.382 --> 01:50:40.717
FOLLOWING HIS TEACHER'S FOOTSTEPS

01:50:40.800 --> 01:50:43.136
AND IS STILL CONSIDERED
THE STRONGEST PLAYER IN HISTORY.

01:50:47.057 --> 01:50:49.893
THE TEACHER AND THE STUDENT

01:50:49.976 --> 01:50:53.813
ARE STILL ACTIVELY PLAYING.
